# docx Library — DOCX Generation Rules

## Core Concepts

The `docx` library generates .docx files (OOXML) declaratively in both Node.js and browser. The API is class-based — you construct a tree of objects, then pack them into a buffer or blob.

## Document Structure

```tsx
import {
  Document, Packer, Paragraph, TextRun, HeadingLevel,
  Table, TableRow, TableCell, WidthType, AlignmentType,
  BorderStyle, ShadingType, ImageRun, ExternalHyperlink,
  Tab, TabStopType, TabStopPosition,
} from "docx";

const doc = new Document({
  creator: "CVFairy",
  title: "Resume — Jane Doe",
  description: "Generated by CVFairy",
  styles: {
    default: {
      document: {
        run: { font: "Calibri", size: 22 }, // size is in half-points: 22 = 11pt
      },
    },
  },
  sections: [
    {
      properties: {
        page: {
          margin: { top: 720, right: 720, bottom: 720, left: 720 }, // twips: 720 = 0.5in
          size: { width: 12240, height: 15840 }, // Letter size in twips
        },
      },
      children: [
        new Paragraph({
          heading: HeadingLevel.HEADING_1,
          children: [new TextRun({ text: "Jane Doe", bold: true })],
        }),
      ],
    },
  ],
});
```

## Units — Critical to Get Right

| Unit | Used for | Conversion |
|------|----------|------------|
| **Half-points** | `size` on TextRun (font size) | 22 = 11pt, 24 = 12pt |
| **Twips** (DXA) | Margins, spacing, cell widths | 1440 = 1 inch, 720 = 0.5in |
| **EMU** | Image dimensions | 914400 = 1 inch |
| **Percentage** | WidthType.PERCENTAGE | 100 = 100% (use with WidthType.PERCENTAGE) |

## Paragraph and TextRun Formatting

```tsx
new Paragraph({
  alignment: AlignmentType.LEFT,
  spacing: { before: 120, after: 60 }, // twips
  indent: { left: 360 }, // twips
  children: [
    new TextRun({ text: "Bold text", bold: true, size: 24 }),
    new TextRun({ text: " and ", size: 24 }),
    new TextRun({ text: "italic", italics: true, size: 24 }),
    new TextRun({ text: " with color", color: "2563EB", size: 24 }),
  ],
});
```

### TextRun Properties
- `bold`, `italics`, `underline: {}`, `strike: true`
- `size` (half-points), `font` (string), `color` (hex without #)
- `superScript`, `subScript`
- `allCaps`, `smallCaps`
- `highlight` (predefined colors: "yellow", "green", etc.)
- `shading: { fill: "EEEEEE", type: ShadingType.CLEAR }`

## Tables

```tsx
const table = new Table({
  columnWidths: [4680, 4680], // twips — MUST set at table level
  rows: [
    new TableRow({
      tableHeader: true, // marks as repeating header row
      children: [
        new TableCell({
          width: { size: 4680, type: WidthType.DXA }, // ALSO set on each cell
          shading: { fill: "E2E8F0", type: ShadingType.CLEAR }, // ALWAYS use ShadingType.CLEAR
          children: [
            new Paragraph({
              alignment: AlignmentType.CENTER,
              children: [new TextRun({ text: "Header", bold: true, size: 22 })],
            }),
          ],
        }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
});
```

### Table Rules
- **Always set `columnWidths` at the table level AND `width` on each cell** — inconsistency causes misaligned columns
- **Always use `ShadingType.CLEAR`** for cell shading — other types can produce black backgrounds in Word
- **A cell MUST end with a Paragraph** — if the last child isn't a Paragraph, one is auto-appended
- **Use `tableHeader: true`** on header rows to repeat them across pages
- **`rowSpan` must be > 1** — rowSpan of 1 crashes Word by adding RESTART without CONTINUE
- Colors are hex strings WITHOUT the `#` prefix: `"2563EB"` not `"#2563EB"`

## Hyperlinks

```tsx
new Paragraph({
  children: [
    new ExternalHyperlink({
      link: "https://example.com",
      children: [
        new TextRun({
          text: "Visit Website",
          style: "Hyperlink", // applies default hyperlink styling
        }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
});
```

## Bullet Lists and Numbering

```tsx
const doc = new Document({
  numbering: {
    config: [
      {
        reference: "bullet-list",
        levels: [
          {
            level: 0,
            format: LevelFormat.BULLET,
            text: "\u2022",
            alignment: AlignmentType.LEFT,
            style: { paragraph: { indent: { left: 360, hanging: 180 } } },
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  sections: [{
    children: [
      new Paragraph({
        numbering: { reference: "bullet-list", level: 0 },
        children: [new TextRun("First bullet point")],
      }),
    ],
  }],
});
```

## Tab Stops (for right-aligned dates)

```tsx
new Paragraph({
  tabStops: [{ type: TabStopType.RIGHT, position: TabStopPosition.MAX }],
  children: [
    new TextRun({ text: "Software Engineer", bold: true }),
    new TextRun({ children: [new Tab(), "Jan 2022 — Present"] }),
  ],
});
```

## Client-Side Download

```tsx
async function downloadDocx(doc: Document, filename: string): Promise<void> {
  const buffer = await Packer.toBuffer(doc);
  const blob = new Blob([buffer], {
    type: "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document",
  });
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  const link = document.createElement("a");
  link.href = url;
  link.download = filename;
  document.body.appendChild(link);
  link.click();
  document.body.removeChild(link);
  URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
}
```

### Client-Side Rules
- Use `Packer.toBuffer()` for browser — produces `Uint8Array`
- Use `Packer.toStream()` for server/Node.js with large documents (100+ pages) — reduces memory by 90%
- Always `URL.revokeObjectURL()` after download to prevent memory leaks
- Wrap generation in `try/catch` — invalid image dimensions or corrupt data cause silent failures
- Test across Word, LibreOffice, and Google Docs — rendering can vary

## Style Definitions

Define reusable styles at the document level:

```tsx
const doc = new Document({
  styles: {
    default: {
      heading1: {
        run: { font: "Calibri", size: 32, bold: true, color: "1E293B" },
        paragraph: { spacing: { before: 240, after: 120 } },
      },
      heading2: {
        run: { font: "Calibri", size: 26, bold: true, color: "334155" },
        paragraph: { spacing: { before: 200, after: 80 } },
      },
      document: {
        run: { font: "Calibri", size: 22, color: "333333" },
        paragraph: { spacing: { line: 276 } }, // 1.15 line spacing (276 = 115% of 240)
      },
    },
  },
  // ...
});
```

## Component-Based Architecture

Mirror the PDF template pattern — create reusable builder functions:

```tsx
function buildExperienceSection(experiences: Experience[]): Paragraph[] {
  return experiences.flatMap((exp) => [
    new Paragraph({
      tabStops: [{ type: TabStopType.RIGHT, position: TabStopPosition.MAX }],
      children: [
        new TextRun({ text: exp.title, bold: true, size: 22 }),
        new TextRun({ children: [new Tab(), `${exp.startDate} — ${exp.endDate}`], size: 20 }),
      ],
    }),
    ...exp.bullets.map(
      (bullet) =>
        new Paragraph({
          numbering: { reference: "bullet-list", level: 0 },
          children: [new TextRun({ text: bullet, size: 22 })],
        }),
    ),
  ]);
}
```

## Gotchas
- Font sizes are **half-points**: for 11pt, use `size: 22`
- Margins and spacing are **twips**: 1 inch = 1440 twips
- Hex colors have **no # prefix**: `"2563EB"` not `"#2563EB"`
- `ShadingType.CLEAR` is required to prevent black cell backgrounds
- Empty arrays in `children` auto-append an empty paragraph
- `Packer.toBuffer()` is async — always await it
